5.179.m:
The seers said:
Tell us, O Sūta, the names of all the officiating priests;
and tell us, O Sūta, what office was assigned to whom there.

Sūta said:
Bhṛgu was then chosen by him for the office of hotṛ, O best of brahmins;
and the sage Cyavana likewise for that named maitrāvaruṇa.

5.180.m:
Madhyaga said:
"Abandoning divine nature, you have resorted to human form;
so how can those foremost twice-born come near you?

5.182.m:
he shall not suffer misfortune for seven rebirths,
especially from bhūtas, pretas, piśācas, and śākinīs;
[there will be] no vulnerability, no diseases, no mental distress, and no fear of enemies.
